# Catalogue content

Author definitions as JSON documents (one file per entity):

- Response / Modify → `src/server/content/cards/<card-id>.json`
- Fighters (engine type creature) → `src/server/content/creatures/<creature-id>.json`
- Named faces → `src/server/content/faces/<face-id>.json`
- One shared deck per team → `src/server/content/loadouts/<id>.json`

JSON must satisfy `src/server/content/schema/*.schema.json`. Inspect the
schema before adding a field. The source is `docs/GAME_STATE.md`. Layer
procedure: `.cursor/skills/author-content/design.md`. Where that note and
this rule disagree, `docs/GAME_STATE.md` wins.

Id constants stay in `cards.ts` / `creatures.ts` / `faces.ts`.
Effects are data, compiled by `AstCompiler`.

Rules:

- Read `docs/KEYWORDS.md` before `rulesText` or effect data. The change is
  not done when they disagree. User-supplied print stays verbatim.
- `type` is `response` or `modify`. `[Block N]`, `[Counter]`, `[Parry]`, and
  redirect are effects. Dodge is not current print. `modifySubject` is
  `roll`, `die`, `moveset`, `target`, or `tag`. Do not author Instant,
  Reaction, Overload, or Ritual as the card kind. A moveset Modify attaches
  in the equipment zone. That is not a card type.
- Faces are named inputs (name, type, primary, secondary). No generic Guard,
  Block, Dodge, Counter, or Parry face. The `face-natural|synthetic|untyped-`
  id prefix is a validator token, not a kind. No Shield resource. No
  deckbuilding dice. `baseDie` on the Fighter is the die a match starts from.
- `fighterRestriction` is a play check, not a deck ban. One deck and one hand
  per player. Tag is an operation. Assist is Fighter-owned.
- Lifecycle is `one-shot` or `persistent`. Meter is exceptional
  (`exceptionalMeterCost`), not mana on every strong card.
- Prefer `[Mark N X]` / `[Strip N X]` / `[Modify]`. Do not print `[Forge]`,
  `[Requires]`, `[Spend]`, `[Generate]`, `[Empower]`, `[Pierce]`,
  `[Convert]`, `[Desynthesize]`, or an attribute-only verb.
- Structured fields only when every clause is modelled. Gaps go to
  `docs/DEFERRED_CATALOGUE.md`.
- Schemas may still require `forge` or `attacks`. Satisfy them. Do not
  design the card around those fields.
- Print voice is the holder: `you` / `opponent`.
- Follow `.cursor/skills/author-content/SKILL.md`.
- Live JSON is catalogue truth. `docs/MECHANIC_ARCHETYPES.md` is not a source.
